        <mxCell id="s11__2" value="Block Functions &amp;amp; Interfaces (notes outside the block diagram)&lt;br&gt;TOP (can_top): host access, RX synchronizer, read-data selection; connects register bank, bit timing, and protocol processing.&lt;br&gt;Source: can_top.v:214, 443-737, 743-869.&lt;br&gt;CAN operation: 11/29-bit identifiers, up to 8 data bytes, CRC-15, arbitration and error confinement are implemented in child RTL;&lt;br&gt;protocol conformance was not simulated.&lt;br&gt;Host strobes rd_i and wr_i are active high. CAN_WISHBONE_IF is not defined in the supplied can_defines.v; optional Wishbone is&lt;br&gt;described in rtl_analysis.md.&lt;br&gt;Dashed thick arrows: functional/interface association; direction of individual bidirectional host/CAN signals is specified by the&lt;br&gt;annotations." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#FFFFFF;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1" vlsit_library_sha256="D1631ACF98A920526B235E8970FEDDC9305EA2F0D6A35C6529CD220D62AFABB6" vlsit_library_entry="32" vlsit_library_cell="2" vlsit_library_instance="s11">
