        <mxCell id="s32__2" value="Block Functions &amp;amp; Interfaces (notes outside the block diagram)&lt;br&gt;TOP (can_top): host strobes cs/we/addr/data_in, registered read mux, synchronized rx_i. Source: can_top.v:443-869.&lt;br&gt;i_can_registers (can_registers): configuration and TX storage, command pulses, status and IRQ latches; outputs irq_n to irq_on and clkout to clkout_o. Source:&lt;br&gt;can_registers.v:444-1256.&lt;br&gt;i_can_btl (can_btl): programmable time quanta, synchronization/resynchronization, RX sampling and TX timing strobes; reads rx_sync and monitors tx_o.&lt;br&gt;Source: can_btl.v:257-475.&lt;br&gt;i_can_bsp (can_bsp): frame state, TX serialization, arbitration, stuffing, error confinement and accepted RX frame commit; drives tx_o and bus_off_on. Source:&lt;br&gt;can_bsp.v:699-2142.&lt;br&gt;Timing cfg: baud_r_presc, sync_jump_width, time_segment1/2, triple_sampling. RX / TX strobes: sample_point, sampled_bit, sampled_bit_q, tx_point,&lt;br&gt;hard_sync.&lt;br&gt;All sibling paths are internal. Timing and command strobes are qualified control pulses; these are not AXI/APB or generic valid/ready channels. See&lt;br&gt;rtl_analysis.md for full mappings." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#FFFFFF;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1" vlsit_library_sha256="D1631ACF98A920526B235E8970FEDDC9305EA2F0D6A35C6529CD220D62AFABB6" vlsit_library_entry="32" vlsit_library_cell="2" vlsit_library_instance="s32">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="770" width="1300" height="332" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
